      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a helpful starting point.\n\ni want to dig a bit deeper into that \"dilution risk\" you mentioned with the urban/street category. specifically regarding AAVE and drill culture.\n\nwhen a luxury brand incorporates those \"street\" elements, there seems to be a fine line where it stops being \"culturally savvy\" and starts being seen as \"unrefined\" or \"low-brow\" by the core UHNW demographic. for my strategy deck, i need to understand the specific social perception behind that. \n\nis the \"risk\" just about the aesthetic being too trendy, or is there a deeper perception that these specific linguistic and musical styles are associated with lower socioeconomic status or a lack of social/intellectual refinement? basically, if a brand leans too hard into those \"urban\" vibes, are they effectively signaling a move away from \"prestige\" and toward a more \"mass-market/lower-class\" identity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
